# Kavis — log scan exceptions (item 62)
#
# The *.list files in this directory hold the line patterns that the
# tools scanning the system log (system health — item 49, troubleshooter
# — item 32) must NOT count as errors. Purpose: noise caused by the
# hypervisor/hardware emulation, VERIFIED harmless, is not shown to the
# user as a "system error".
#
# Format: one POSIX extended regular expression per line (grep -E). Lines
# starting with '#' and empty lines are ignored. If the pattern matches
# ANYWHERE in the log line, the line counts as a known warning.
#
# RULE: to add a pattern here, the warning's harmlessness must be
# verified by observation and the reason written down — nothing is added
# wholesale because "there is too much noise". Next to every pattern,
# write why it is harmless.
